`flushJobs(seed, expand, maxJobs)` models one synchronous update cycle. `seed` must be an array of strings, `expand` a function, and `maxJobs` a non-negative safe integer; malformed arguments throw `TypeError`. Process jobs in FIFO order. For each processed job, call `expand(job)`, which must return an array of strings or cause a `TypeError`. Append generated jobs to the same queue so they are eligible for processing during the current call. Stop only when the queue is exhausted or `maxJobs` jobs have been processed.

Return `{ processed, pending }`, each a new array. `processed` contains handled jobs in order; `pending` contains all remaining queued jobs in order. With `maxJobs` equal to zero, all seed jobs are pending. Do not mutate `seed` or any array returned by `expand`; strings eliminate nested aliasing concerns. Export exactly `{ flushJobs }` using CommonJS.

